<BaseLayout title="About New York Cryogen | AC-130 Viper" description="Learn about New York Cryogen and founder Gregory Papageorge, the company developing AC-130 Viper.">
  <main>
    <section class="sub-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / ABOUT THE COMPANY</p>
        <h1>The people behind the development.</h1>
        <p>New York Cryogen, Inc. is developing the AC-130 Viper technology platform.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section"><div class="container split-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">OUR STORY</p><h2>A development journey rooted in experience</h2><p>New York Cryogen was founded by Gregory Papageorge. According to the company’s published history, his experience working in medical technology and his personal experience with chronic pain helped inspire the exploration of localized cooling technology.</p><p>Today, the public development focus includes engineering, testing, quality preparation and regulatory work.</p></div><figure class="content-image"><img src="/images/ny-cryogen-studio.jpg" alt="New York Cryogen company branding and development workspace" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" /></figure></div></section>
    <section class="content-section light-section"><div class="container prose-narrow"><p class="eyebrow">OUR FOCUS</p><h2>Purposeful product development</h2><p>The AC-130 Viper is not commercially available in the United States. This website provides company background and development updates rather than treatment recommendations or an offer to purchase a medical device.</p><a class="text-link" href="/media/">Explore interviews and podcasts ↗</a></div></section>

    <section class="sub-cta">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">STAY CONNECTED</p>
        <h2>Follow the development of AC-130 Viper.</h2>
        <p>For product-development, company, business or media inquiries, contact New York Cryogen.</p>
        <a class="button-primary" href="/contact/">Contact New York Cryogen ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
